# Implementation Plan

## Phase 0: Foundation

- [x] Rust arithmetic DAG and deterministic scheduler; tests and benchmark CLI.
- [x] Apache-2.0 license, contributor and security policies.
- [x] Hosted CI and public repository approval.

## Phase 1: Evaluator (days 2–4)

- [x] Freeze reference arithmetic and public development workloads; check fixed outputs and necessary cycle bounds (#4).
- [x] Add negative controls and reference comparisons for public fixtures (#4).
- [x] Implement reviewer-side corpus validation, public fixture separation checks and digest protocol (#5).
- [ ] Independent custodian prepares, isolates, verifies and seals a real withheld corpus before candidate search (#5).

## Phase 2: Search (days 5–7)

- [ ] Deterministic candidate search and content-addressed experiment ledger.
- [ ] Record cycles, wall time, resource usage, tool/source hashes, seeds and failures.
- [ ] Cap each batch at 100 software, 10 RTL and two routed candidates initially; agents propose structural changes, deterministic algorithms search parameters.

## Phase 3: RTL (week 2)

- [ ] SystemVerilog baseline, independent reference comparison, reset/backpressure tests.
- [ ] Validate Cora Z7-07S configuration and routed Vivado timing/resource reports.
- [ ] Evaluate formal tools with a bounded feasibility experiment.

## Phase 4: Hardware (week 3)

- [ ] Verify finalist improvement on independent workloads; record model/RTL cycles, routed frequency and LUT/FF/BRAM/DSP usage.
- [ ] Operator-approved physical test and reproducible evidence; distinguish estimated power from measured energy.

## Phase 5: Public Alpha (week 4)

- [ ] Locked build, tests, lint, CLI reproduction and graph integrity on supported hosts.
- [ ] Review source for secrets, private data, upstream licenses and security risks.
- [ ] Prepare the initial SemVer release PR, verify Cargo version and lockfile, date the changelog entry, and obtain maintainer approval for a matching immutable tag; publish tutorial and evidence (#9).
- [ ] Validate demand with hardware researchers and small engineering teams; evaluate integration, custom optimization and support.

Target windows are planning assumptions. Release a clearly labeled simulator alpha if hardware slips; no unverified performance or market-leadership claims. Defer custom ISA, OS, ASIC and full interaction-net runtime until justified.

## Verify

